**What was wrong:**

| Bug | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| **Overselling** | `check_stock` → `charge` → `decrement` — three separate async calls with no atomicity. Between check and decrement, other coroutines also passed the check and all charged successfully. `decrement`'s own guard couldn't save it because the window between checking `self._stock` and writing was wide open. | Added `check_and_decrement(quantity)` to `Inventory` — atomically checks and decrements under an `asyncio.Lock`. Only one coroutine can hold the lock and pass the stock check at a time, so stock can never go negative. |
| **Ghost charges** | When `decrement` failed after a successful charge, the code printed an error but the customer's money was already charged — no item delivered, no record, no refund. | `checkout` now reserves stock first (via `check_and_decrement`). If `charge` subsequently fails, `increment(quantity)` restores the reserved stock immediately. Every charge always has a corresponding item. |
| **Duplicate charges** | Not observed in the original bug, but possible if the same `order_id` was reused — now structurally impossible since stock reservation is exclusive. | N/A — structural fix. |
